# atomic sandbox scene v1
# Hydrogen molecule at R = 1.45 Bohr (Bohr): this solver's sigma -> 0 LSDA bond length (1.4511,
# crates/validate/references.md), i.e. the physical starting geometry. It vibrates when you press
# Play because the nuclear smearing (sigma = h) moves the minimum outward: 1.60 Bohr at the
# default Accurate quality (h = 0.15), 1.79 at Balanced (0.25) — the start is that far compressed.
grid 49 0.25
charge 0
nucleus 1  0.725 0 0
nucleus 1 -0.725 0 0
